    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec: reject creating an owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, responding **409 Conflict**.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I mirrored the existing pattern in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 which already delegates each business rule to a small, cohesive helper class (`Households`, `CityCodes`, `Namesakes`, etc.) rather than inlining logic into the controller.\n\n1. **New helper `Emails.java`** \u2014 a tiny, self-contained class (WMC_other \u2248 0) holding the email-uniqueness rule: normalize (trim, lowercase, treat blank as absent) and compare case-insensitively against existing owners. Owners without an email never clash.\n\n2. **Two-line guard in `addOwner`** \u2014 one `if (Emails.isDuplicate(owners, owner))` returning `CONFLICT`, placed alongside the sibling duplicate checks. The changed method's own complexity stays flat, and the heavy logic lives outside the large controller class.\n\nThe dedicated acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
